[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138109,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Glioneuronal hamartoma of the ciliary body is a tumour-like neuroglial lesion occurring at the margin of the optic cup, often with an adjacent chorioretinal coloboma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138110,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138111,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LA11.Y Other specified structural developmental anomalies of the anterior segment of eye</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138112,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> glioneuroma of the ciliary body.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138113,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138114,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Localization is in the ciliary body, typically in the temporal quadrant, with frequent extension to the iris and retina {6703991;2622623;4697214;4697215}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138115,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions appear as a tan, slowly growing mass, usually detected before the first year of life, often at birth. Extraocular extension may be present {4697215;2622623}. A chorioretinal coloboma may coexist but not be clinically detectable {2622623;4697215}. The eye may secondarily be smaller or larger than the contralateral eye, the cornea and lens may be cloudy {4697215;6703991}, a persistent pupillary membrane or hyaloid artery may be present {4697214;4697215}, and the intraocular pressure may be elevated {2622623;4697215}. The tumour enhances with contrast medium on CT {2622623}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138116,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions are very rare. Fewer than 10&nbsp;cases have been published {6703991;2622623;4697214;4697215}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138117,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions arise as a congenital developmental mass {2622623;4697215}. There is no association with neurofibromatosis type&nbsp;1 or&nbsp;2.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138118,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>One possibility is that the developing choristoma interferes with the normal development of the adjacent iris, ciliary body, choroid, and retina, and causes a secondary coloboma. Alternatively, faulty differentiation of the optic cup could result in formation of both heterotopic brain tissue and a coloboma {2622623}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138119,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions appear as a pink, greyish, or yellowish mass in the ciliary body.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138120,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour consists of fibrillary astrocytes, an eosinophilic matrix of glial and neuronal processes, clusters of neuronal cells with small round nuclei, and scattered large ganglion cells. Calcospherites, dysplastic rosettes, and tubules composed of several rows of cells that resemble Homer Wright and Flexner&ndash;Wintersteiner rosettes may be present. Mitotic figures are very rare or absent. The glial component is immunopositive for GFAP and the neuronal component for synaptophysin and neurofilament proteins {2622623}. The ciliary epithelium over the mass shows reactive proliferation. The adjacent retina may be dysplastic and may extend to the chorioretinal coloboma when one is present {2622623;4697215}. Glioneuroma of the ciliary body must be distinguished from teratoid medulloepithelioma containing mature brain tissue {655220;2622623;4697214}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138121,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 117,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not reported</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
